# Template for ~/.pi-setup.env — the machine-local secret file.
#
# install.sh / install.ps1 copies this to ~/.pi-setup.env (mode 600) when that
# file does not exist yet, then fills in the values you paste. The live file
# lives OUTSIDE this repository, so a secret can never be committed here or
# reach the public mirror.
#
# Why this file exists: Pi registers a provider only when its documented
# environment variable is set. Every model in settings.json whose provider is
# unregistered makes each subagent launch print
#   [pi-subagents] Skipping fallback model '<id>' because it is unavailable...
#
# Fill in only the providers you actually use. Leave the rest commented out.
# Variable names come from the Pi docs: docs/providers.md.

# Z.ai Coding Plan — provider id `zai`, used by settings.json fallback chains
# and by the architect-glm / tester-glm roles.
# Note: Pi reads ZAI_API_KEY. The Z.ai Vision MCP server reads Z_AI_API_KEY.
# Set this one; scripts/pi-env.sh mirrors it to the other name automatically.
# ZAI_API_KEY=

# Anthropic — provider id `anthropic`. Only needed for API-key auth;
# `pi auth` OAuth login writes ~/.pi/agent/auth.json instead.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Google Gemini — provider id `google`.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Amazon Bedrock — provider id `amazon-bedrock`.
# AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK=
